<title>HUNGARY: Hungarian central bank cuts rates on bank reserves.</title>
<headline>Hungarian central bank cuts rates on bank reserves.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Thursday it will reduce the interest rate it pays to commercial banks on their forint reserves made upon foreign currency sources to an annual 18.00 percent from 19.50 percent.</p>
<p>The reduction is effective from October 16, the NBH said in a statement.</p>
<p>The NBH left other rates unchanged.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
